<title>UK: UK reserves fall underlying $26 mln in May.</title>
<headline>UK reserves fall underlying $26 mln in May.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's gold and currency reserves fell an underlying $26 million in May, the Treasury said. </p>
<p>(IN MLN DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>					  May		    April</p>
<p> Underlying reserves	     - 26		    - 93</p>
<p>  Actual reserves		  - 43		    - 105</p>
<p> Total actual reserves	 40.57 billion	 40.61 billion</p>
<p>The underlying change excludes factors included in the total</p>
<p>change (IN MLN OF DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED) -</p>
<p>Repayments under the</p>
<p> exchange cover scheme (ECS)     16			88</p>
<p>--London Forex Desk +44 171 542 6762</p>
</text>
